# DnB mix sessions

Hard-won from the October 2026 listening sessions. Full findings also live in `docs/mixing.md` ("Listening-session findings").

## Before planning — screen the pool

- Screening is built in since 2026-10: the planning pool excludes unstable grids (`PLANNER_MIN_TEMPO_STABILITY = 0.6`, see `packages/domain/src/constants.ts`), grid-phase suspects (confidence-aware), and owner-rated-1 tracks. Manually exclude only for diagnosed cases not covered by those gates — read the constants from code, not from this file, so advice can't drift.
- Prefer tracks with an early first drop (≤ ~110s) or 2+ drops. Single-late-drop tracks produce source-0 entries ("energy dies") or sub-90s bodies (render fails "no native body").
- Structure queries: `track_sections` (type/start_ms), stability from the latest `dnb-crate-dsp` analysis row.

## After planning — audit before rendering

- Reject any join whose incoming starts near source 0 with a drumless head (intro energy < 0.05). Fix by drop-anchoring: mix-in = drop start − overlap, snapped to the incoming's downbeat grid.
- Gallop signature: 32-bar phrase_mix between two busy break patterns. **Listening guidance, not an automated rule** — automation swaps only on the decisive kick-placement trigger (`PLANNER_BASS_SWAP_TRIGGER_GROOVE = -0.45`) and crossfades structural conflicts. When the ear confirms gallop, `transition:compare` the 16-bar bass_swap variant before converting.
- Verify all joins with the beat-train predictor (`storedGridFromEvidence` from `packages/catalog/src/render/check-metrics.ts` fed analysis beats + plan windows). Iterate seeds/exclusions until clean; only then render.
- After rendering: `render:check`, and read per-join residuals from the manifest — the predictor and checker occasionally disagree; the checker is the authority. Deck-probe findings are advisory (`scope: "source-decks"`); see `docs/rendering.md` for the four verification signals.

## Editing plans

- Use `updateSetPlan` (`replaceTrack`, `setTransition`, `setTrim`, `applyTransition`) — never raw `buildEntries` (it re-derives windows and can balloon a plan to 76 minutes).
- `applyTransition` only sets `incomingSourceEndMs` on the LAST entry; trim middle entries with `setTrim` separately.
- Window edits through `updateSetPlan` strip stale alignment pins automatically (and the entry builder no longer re-stamps `recipeVersion` on those joins). Only raw plan-JSON edits must strip `downbeatOffsetMs`/`alignmentMode`/`alignmentPeriodMs`/`onsetLockBeats`/`recipeVersion` by hand.
- Phase nudges: shift the incoming's start by the measured residual; for drop-anchored incomings prefer shifting the OUTGOING's end so the drop landing stays pinned. Search ±40..160 empirically and re-verify.

## Owner preferences (Arild)

- 172–176 BPM; high-energy or liquid hours both welcome.
- Club-style pacing: 90–150s tools are good, explicitly endorsed. Do not enforce long plays.
- Loves phrase_mix 32b joins; bass_swap 16b is the gallop antidote.
- Hates: drumless-intro entries, energy dips between tracks, tracks that overstay (3:40+ mid-set), galloping overlaps.
- "Unmixable" verdicts: move the file to `C:\Users\arild\Music\unmixable\`, `library:scan`, rate the track 1 with the diagnosis in notes (and add the id + reason to `data/session-offenders.json`), and record a `feedback:rate` row. That registry file is a local, optional human-readable record — not a setup requirement; the ratings are what the pool reads.
- **Briefs set `minRating: 2` and rate offenders 1 in the catalog.** `minRating` is null-safe in the planning pool since 2026-10: unrated tracks pass, only explicitly-rated-bad are excluded. Search's `minRating` stays rated-only browsing — do not "fix" it to match.
- Keeper copies of final mixes: transcode the listen FLAC with ffmpeg to 256k AAC (`.m4a`) named `<mix>-keeper.m4a` in `output/renders/`.
- After adding test files, run `tsc --noEmit -p <package>/tsconfig.json` (tests are included there) — vitest does not typecheck, and windows-smoke will catch it otherwise.
